// Title: Potential Chrome Frame Helper DLL Sideloading
// Sigma ID: 72ca7c75-bf85-45cd-aca7-255d360e423c
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), Wietze Beukema (project and research)
// Date: 2022-08-17 | Modified: 2023-05-15
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects potential DLL sideloading of "chrome_frame_helper.dll"
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://hijacklibs.net/entries/3rd_party/google/chrome_frame_helper.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_chrome_frame_helper.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\chrome_frame_helper.dll" and (not((FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Google\\Chrome\\Application\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Google\\Chrome\\Application\\"))) and (not(FolderPath contains "\\AppData\\local\\Google\\Chrome\\Application\\"))
